# Who must look at changes to the files that set the rules for agents and people.
# The owner asked for these paths to be protected (summary of 2026-11-05, recorded on #685).
#
# This file requests the owner's review of a pull request that touches a protected path. It does
# not block a merge: the `main` ruleset does not require code-owner review, because agents open
# pull requests through the owner's own GitHub account and GitHub does not let an author approve
# their own pull request. Enforcement waits for agents to have their own identity (#106).
# Until then the rule that agents never change their own guardrails rests on AGENTS.md, the
# independent review, which lists every policy change.
#
# Changing this file is itself a policy change.

